Modified electric harpsichords (often dubbed "Chroma-Clavichords"), heavily fuzzed-out hollow-body electric guitars with impossibly long sustain circuits, '50s-era tube amplifiers with custom tremolo and spring reverb tanks, minimalist percussive loops derived from decaying jazz drum samples, bass played on a detuned baritone guitar or a bowed double bass filtered through tape saturation units, and custom-built analog looping modules designed to emulate corrupted tape feedback.

